---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE, TOOLS } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumb, webPage } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'About';
const description =
	'VendorDesk builds free, client-side browser tools for small businesses, designers and packaging specialists — no paywalls, no sign-ups, nothing uploaded.';

const schema = [
	webPage({ name: title, path: '/about', description, type: 'AboutPage', hasBreadcrumb: true }),
	breadcrumb([
		{ name: 'Home', path: '/' },
		{ name: 'About', path: '/about' },
	]),
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="About"
		title="Fast tools for people who do their own billing, printing and shipping."
		lead="VendorDesk is a small, independent project with one purpose: replace the bloated, gated calculators that independent businesses are forced to use with browser tools that are instant, private and free."
		crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About' }]}
	/>

	<section class="bg-canvas">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-prose px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24">
			<div class="rich-text">
				<h2 class="mt-0!">Our mission</h2>
				<p>
					A designer preparing a paper bag for a client should not need a 3D rendering account to get a dieline. A freelancer
					invoicing a retail client should not have to verify an email address and dodge three upsells to download a one-page
					document. These are small, well-defined problems — and small, well-defined problems deserve small, precise tools.
				</p>
				<p>
					VendorDesk exists to build those tools for <strong>independent businesses, digital designers and packaging
					specialists</strong>, and to keep them free of paywalls. Each tool does one job, does it properly, and gets out of
					the way.
				</p>

				<h2>How we build</h2>
				<h3>Client-side by design</h3>
				<p>
					Every VendorDesk tool runs completely in your web browser. The die-line SVG is drawn by JavaScript on your machine;
					the Bill of Supply PDF is assembled on your machine. We have no server that receives your inputs, which means we
					cannot lose, leak or sell your packaging dimensions, client names or amounts — because we never have them.
				</p>
				<h3>Static and fast</h3>
				<p>
					The site is generated ahead of time as plain HTML and CSS. There are no frameworks hydrating on load, no chat
					bubbles, no cookie banners. Pages are typically interactive in well under a second on a mid-range phone, which is
					where most of our visitors are.
				</p>
				<h3>Honest about limits</h3>
				<p>
					Our tools are precise, but packaging tooling and tax documents both have consequences. We say so plainly on every
					tool page, we explain the maths and the rules we apply, and we ask you to proof a physical mock-up or talk to your
					accountant before you commit. See the <a href="/terms-of-service">terms of service</a>.
				</p>

				<h2>What is live today</h2>
				<ul>
					{
						TOOLS.map((t) => (
							<li>
								<a href={t.href}>{t.name}</a> — {t.description}
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
				<p>
					More single-purpose utilities are on the way. If a repetitive calculation or document is stealing your afternoons,
					<a href="/contact">tell us about it</a> — the tools we build next are chosen from those requests.
				</p>

				<h2>Who is behind VendorDesk</h2>
				<p>
					VendorDesk is built and maintained independently from India by people who have run small design and supply
					businesses themselves. It is not backed by a SaaS company and is not a lead-generation funnel for one. The project is
					supported by unobtrusive advertising so that the tools can stay free for everyone.
				</p>
				<p>
					Questions, corrections or ideas: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
